@startuml phonendo_secuencia
!theme plain
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
title Phonendo — from reading to payment

participant Reader as R
participant Manager as M
participant Verifier as V
participant Storage as S
participant Publisher as P
participant "Soroban contract" as C #E8E6FF
participant "Web panels" as W

== Verification (every reading) ==
M -> R : subscribe to /stream
R --> M : observation (SSE)
note over R,M : Alternative: POST /newEvent; the first transport chosen for a readerId wins.
note over M : Build the Captured event and hash its content.
M -> V : verify event (HTTP /verify)
alt Accepted
  V --> M : Verified event, ed25519 signature
  M -> S : store Verified event
  M --> P : Verified event (SSE /stream)
else Explicit rejection
  V --> M : rejection
  note over M,S : Discard; never stored.
else Timeout
  note over M,S : In-memory queue; retry from the pending stage.
end

== Proof and payment (every 5 readings of one device) ==
note over P
  Collect 5 Verified readings, derive sessionId from their event ids, pick a random salt.
  Generate the Groth16 proof (circuits/): at least minCount
  readings are inside [minValue, maxValue].
end note
P -> M : POST /signBatch (sessionId, salt, patient, 5 event ids)
M -> V : POST /signBatch
note over V
  Checks sessionId against the event ids and that
  no event was signed in another session.
  Takes the readings from its own memory,
  computes Poseidon(sessionId, salt, readings)
  and signs it with ed25519.
end note
V --> M : commitment + signature
M --> P : commitment + signature
note over P : Rejects the signature if the commitment differs from its proof.
P -> C : claim(patient, sessionId, commitment, signature, proof)
note over C
  1. Session not paid before (anti-replay)
  2. Verifier signature (host ed25519)
  3. Groth16 proof against the stored policy (BLS12-381)
end note
C -> C : mark session, transfer USDC to the patient (or carrier)
C --> W : SessionPaid event
W -> W : show the payment and its transaction on stellar.expert
@enduml
